      "content": "For the Tokyo to Osaka leg, a buffer of about 60 to 90 minutes between Shinkansen stations is usually sufficient, as transfers at major hubs like Kobe or Chiba are well-organized though uncommon on direct routes. However, traveling from Osaka to Fukuoka cannot be done entirely by Shinkansen requiring just one pass, as no single bullet train connects them directly. Consequently, buying individual tickets or just purchasing a JR Pass for the first leg without covering the second leg is typically smarter for most travelers. Since you won't be chaining three double-chinkansen rides, the cumulative cost savings from a 7-day or 14-day pass will likely be negligible compared to buying ticket bundles or individual fares.",
